  "summary": "Chandler, Arizona's City Council delayed until July a vote on renewing a $153,000+ contract with Flock Safety for its 40-camera ALPR network after hours of debate and public protest. Police cited stolen-vehicle recoveries, missing persons located, and arrests, while opponents and some council members raised surveillance and oversight concerns.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I have major problems with that because that's oversight. That is our job to look to make sure\u2014I'm not trying to make a spectacle of anything. I'm just simply trying to protect our privacy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "the city of Chandler owns 100% of its data under the terms of the contract and controls whether to share that data",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
